```java
public int cardinality() {
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < wordsInUse; i++)
            sum += Long.bitCount(words[i]);
        return sum;
        // @@@ The number of bits set to true in this BitSet is always greater than or equal to 0.
    }
```

We need to output an assert statement that reflects that the number of bits set to true is always >= 0.

We need to use \result for return value. So assert \result >= 0;

